  "caption": "Quinn heard a friend got dry needled and pictured a full pincushion situation. Kay had a calmer explanation.\n\nDry needling uses a thin, solid needle in a tight, tender muscle, with nothing injected. It may ease pain in the short term, but lasting change mostly comes from progressive exercise, so it works best as one part of a bigger plan.\n\nA few tips: use the calmer window to get your exercises going, keep moving gently if you're a bit sore for a day or two, ask what the plan is beyond the session, and don't judge it by whether a muscle twitched.\n\nChest pain or breathlessness after a session, or spreading redness or fever, needs prompt medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
